<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Attack routines of SquishyMelee. Edit, add or remove routines here; the game only has to be restarted (no build).

  A routine is one choreography of an attack, whatever the weapon is. The game deals its blow on one tick only: that tick is time 0 of the
  routine, and the strike of the routine is on it. Everything before it (Pre) leads up to it, everything after it (Post) is what the pawn
  does with the weapon and body once the blow is struck. The body reaction (the soft ring-out) is added on top of all this by the mod and
  never stops, whatever comes next.

  <Routine id weight combo mirror cold kinds>
    id      the name of the routine (a translation key SM_Routine_<id> gives the name shown in the options)
    weight  how likely the routine is chosen (1 = normal, 0 = never); the player can change it in the options
    combo   (not used by the routines that come with the mod: there are no extra strikes; a swing before the blow is part of Pre)
    mirror  true: the weapon swing of this routine alternates from one attack to the next
    cold    false: the routine needs the lead-in of an attack before it (a leap, a deep crouch), it is never the first attack of a fight
    kinds   all, or a list of Slash, Thrust, Smash, Bite: only for weapons whose swing kind is among them

  <Hit>   what happens ON the blow (time 0): the pose the parts are brought to, and how hard the body is kicked
  <Pre>   keys with a negative time (ticks before the blow, the last key at 0): the lead-in that the attack before plays
  <Post>  keys with a positive time (ticks after the blow): what is held or moved to after the blow; the last key is where it stays
          until the lead-in of the next routine takes over (the weapon may stay down, or up, ...)

  Values of a key or of the hit (all optional, 0 when left out), at strength 1:
    sw    weapon swing in degrees, positive = down (clockwise), negative = up/back;  up  weapon held higher, in cells
    wx    weapon pushed forward, in cells;   push  the pawn forward, in cells;   lean  body lean, in degrees (positive = towards the target)
    sy sx body squash (sy: height, sx: width; negative sy = lower);   hop  the pawn lifted (leap), in cells;   head  head turn, in degrees
    shf shr  shield forward (cells) / turn (degrees)
    pt    how much the weapon is turned to point at the target (0 = as it is held, 1 = pointing); for thrusts, so that a sword or an axe
          held at a slant still looks like a stab. In <Hit> it is where the weapon IS at the strike; the angle it means is set per weapon.
  A key may have stop="true": the motion comes to rest there (otherwise it flows through the key).
  In <Hit>: sw, up are where the weapon IS at the strike; the others are kicks that ring out. landing: squash on landing after a leap.
  <Strike gap amp arc push hold pull>: gap ticks after the previous strike; amp size; arc 1 same / -1 opposite swing; push size of the dash;
          hold ticks of hit stop; pull how far it is drawn back right before it.
-->
<Routines>
